then you need to reign in your mind, hold\h\h

173
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:52,799
it hold it back from that, and then once that\h
calmes down you would be able to recognize what's\h\h

174
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:58,799
already there. Because again, it's like that that\h
simile that the Buddha gave, when the\h\h

175
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:06,719
pond has been stirred up and all the mud in the\h
pond is moving around, you can't see what's\h\h

176
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:15,759
underneath. And so the way to still it is not to concentrate on some object that's ironically\h\h

177
00:23:15,760 --> 00:23:22,399
going to be secondary to the physicality;
it's to stop giving in to these unwholesome\h\h

178
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:28,079
activities that may seem totally justified, because
see, I'm trying to practice and all that,\h\h

179
00:23:28,080 --> 00:23:32,559
but again, wholesome and unwholesome\h
is determined by the intention behind it. So\h\h

180
00:23:32,560 --> 00:23:40,239
it's if it's an intention of restlessness and\h
craving, then that will obstruct your clear seeing,\h\h

181
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:51,279
whether you like it or not. But, again, if you haven't abandoned the even coarser\h\h

182
00:23:51,280 --> 00:23:57,919
unwholesome activities, where you're still\h
on account of these pressuring thoughts, acting\h\h

183
00:23:57,920 --> 00:24:05,039
out by body and speech towards sensuality and\h
aversion, then there's no hope that you can

184
00:24:05,040 --> 00:24:11,199
undo the pressures on this mental level. But if all\h
that other stuff has been taken care of beforehand,\h\h

185
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:18,559
then you're just left with this and then it's a\h
matter of applying the same principle that you\h\h

186
00:24:18,560 --> 00:24:26,559
did with your virtue. You didn't try to
prevent the options to break the precepts from\h\h

187
00:24:26,560 --> 00:24:33,279
existing. You don't go out into the world\h
and destroy all the alcohol there is in order\h\h

188
00:24:33,280 --> 00:24:39,519
to keep the precept of not drinking, and so on. While the option to do it is\h\h

189
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:45,039
there you don't give into it. And it's the same\h
when you have these mental pressures. You\h\h

190
00:24:45,040 --> 00:24:52,639
will have the craving to do something,\h
whatever it might be, and in this case to find the\h\h

191
00:24:52,640 --> 00:24:59,119
physicality that's coming through that sense of\h
restlessness and then you don't

192
00:24:59,120 --> 00:25:05,039
try to just remove it, because that's going to be\h
another restlessness, instead you just say: "Okay,\h\h

193
00:25:05,040 --> 00:25:14,079
well, I'll endure this infinitely, because in and of\h
itself it has risen on its own." So if I imply that\h\h

194
00:25:14,080 --> 00:25:22,719
I need to get rid of it, that's going to be taking\h
ownership of it and that's, again, going to obscure\h\h

195
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:32,800
whatever you may need to see. So in a way you\h
could say, when you no longer care\h\h

196
00:25:33,920 --> 00:25:38,329
as much about finding the physicality,\h
that's when you'll be able to do it.

197
00:25:41,028 --> 00:25:45,279
But you certainly need to keep trying\h
to discern it. It's not like you just\h\h

198
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:49,039
throw your hands up in the air and\h
and wait for it to arise. There\h\h

199
00:25:49,040 --> 00:25:55,519
has to be the effort, but you realize ninety-nine procent\h
of the effort is indirect. It's the effort\h\h

200
00:25:55,520 --> 00:26:04,640
of undoing what obstructs the recognition and\h
not just to kind of fabricate the recognition.

201
00:26:06,640 --> 00:26:12,289
So would I be correct to say that it's good to practice...

202
00:26:16,288 --> 00:26:24,879
including these pressuring\h
thoughts of finding the physicality into the\h\h

203
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:32,159
pressure. Yes. Because see, any thought...\h
that's actually the crucial thing,\h\h

204
00:26:32,160 --> 00:26:40,239
because again, if you've been keeping\h
virtue, if you have thoughts about covetousness\h\h

205
00:26:40,240 --> 00:26:49,119
and greed and fantasizing about things\h
you want and hating and being annoyed at\h\h

206
00:26:49,120 --> 00:26:54,319
certain people or whatever, you will recognize\h
those thoughts quite easily and you will\h\h

207
00:26:54,320 --> 00:27:01,279
be able to restrain them. But when it comes to\h
these other things that are slightly more subtle\h\h

208
00:27:01,280 --> 00:27:09,199
and might even feel justified like I said\h
before, most of the time you'll get\h\h

209
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:16,159
dragged by it because it just feels
so personal. It's kind of like you just almost\h\h

210
00:27:16,160 --> 00:27:23,679
automatically take it for granted. So yes, very\h
much it has to be included, because at the end of\h\h

211
00:27:23,680 --> 00:27:34,959
the day a pressure is a pressure. So you don't\h
want to be justifying it, or kind of acting as if\h\h

212
00:27:34,960 --> 00:27:41,599
some pressures are fine. If you want to overcome\h
the hindrances, which are what obstructs the\h\h

213
00:27:41,600 --> 00:27:50,159
recognition of the physicality, then you need to be\h
careful with any direction that involves pressure.\h\h

214
00:27:50,160 --> 00:27:56,959
Because that's what the hindrances are. It's
any type of pressure. So there's often\h\h

215
00:27:56,960 --> 00:28:03,519
this tendency for people to justify, like: "No,\h
no, I know that I'm acting out of hindrances,\h\h

216
00:28:03,520 --> 00:28:10,239
but I just hope that if this is kind of
the right acting out, if I just keep going\hthere,

217
00:28:10,240 --> 00:28:17,279
eventually somehow I'll arrive at\h
this thing that I'm looking for."

218
00:28:17,280 --> 00:28:24,559
But that's not a very realistic\h
hope and you basically just wind yourself\h\h

219
00:28:24,560 --> 00:28:31,999
up and take yourself farther away from it, and\h
then at some point\h\h

220
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:39,279
you'll give up on it, and then maybe you'll have\h
the chance to find it. But you can prevent that\h\h

221
00:28:39,280 --> 00:28:45,199
entire thing, you can prevent that entire wasted\h
effort by just from the very beginning realize:\h\h

222
00:28:45,200 --> 00:28:53,119
"Okay, this is a pressure. I shouldn't be acting\h
out of it." Because, again,\h\h

223
00:28:53,120 --> 00:28:55,089
it's not only about the physicality.

224
00:28:55,090 --> 00:29:02,022
If you see\hpressure as pressure, you're also developing
 yoniso manasikāra.

225
00:29:03,120 --> 00:29:09,679
That will be the way towards recognizing all the five\h
holding aggregates, basically. Yes, so if right\h\h

226
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:15,999
now you're being pressured to recognize the body,\hcontemplate what feeling is there.

227
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:22,639
Is it an unpleasant feeling that's there on account of not\h
seeing the body? And if you take it through that\h\h

228
00:29:22,640 --> 00:29:30,319
angle, that's already mindfulness. It may not be the\h
mindfulness you wanted, but that doesn't matter.

229
00:29:30,320 --> 00:29:35,439
Most of the time that's the better mindfulness.\h
Yes. Exactly. It's the one you need, not\h\h

230
00:29:35,440 --> 00:29:43,599
the one you want. So again, being mindful\h
of your intention: "Why am I trying to do this?" And\h\h

231
00:29:43,600 --> 00:29:50,079
that is the proper mindfulness, the proper\h
yoniso manasikāra, then and there. And if you stick to\h\h

232
00:29:50,080 --> 00:29:55,199
it then maybe you will get to see the body\h
on the same peripheral level, but you have\h\h

233
00:29:55,200 --> 00:30:03,920
to be careful that the attempt is, again,\h
not rooted in the same pressure, like we said before.